From: Vahiru <nekovahiru@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] overlay: disable desktop windowing

The common crDroid overlay sets config_isDesktopModeSupported to true
for every device. On the Huawei MateBook E Go this opens apps in
freeform windows. The device overlay cannot turn it off: in this tree
the overlays in PRODUCT_PACKAGE_OVERLAYS, which include this one, take
precedence over DEVICE_PACKAGE_OVERLAYS. Set it to false here.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [device-specific policy]
---
 overlay/common/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/overlay/common/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml b/overlay/common/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml
index a688884..b798f35 100644
--- a/overlay/common/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml
+++ b/overlay/common/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml
@@ -95,7 +95,7 @@
     <bool name="config_battery_percentage_setting_available">false</bool>
 
     <!-- Whether desktop mode is supported on the current device  -->
-    <bool name="config_isDesktopModeSupported">true</bool>
+    <bool name="config_isDesktopModeSupported">false</bool>
 
     <!-- List of packages that can use the Conversation space for their category messages
     notifications until they target R -->
